WEBVTT

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.730
Escha, it's about time you go to bed.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.450
But I'm not sleepy at all!

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:23.370
Miria will get mad at you again if you sleep in and skip alchemy practice again tomorrow.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.960
In that case, tell me a story, Clone.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.340
I'll go to sleep if you do.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.300
A story?

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.860
Yep! A really fun and exciting story!

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.450
That's a difficult order.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.090
I think we might have one.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.710
This is a picture book that I wrote in the past.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.780
You did, Clone?

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.910
Yes, although I didn't expect to read it to anybody.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.660
Am I the first one?

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.780
I'm so looking forward to it!

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.250
Read it to me! Hurry!

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.170
Okay. I'll read it now.

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:15.960
This story is called "The Adventures of the Hummingbird Princess".

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.710
Good morning. It's morning already.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.890
Wake up, Escha.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.700
Yes.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.770
My oh my, you mustn't be late.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.350
Today's your first day on the job, isn't it?

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.230
Yep! I'll do my best!

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.080
Good morning, Escha!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.940
Good morning, Martha-san!

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.540
How are the vegetables today?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.920
The harvest hasn't been going well lately.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.340
I see.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.820
It's the regular balloon flight.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.140
Escha, you are starting today, right?

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.110
Oh, yes.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:21.570
Here, this is to celebrate. Take it.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.490
Good morning!

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.410
And? They gave you this?

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:37.420
I'm sorry, Marion-san, but they said this is to celebrate.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:40.420
If it's to celebrate, we mustn't refuse.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.520
We'll take care of the flowers.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.050
Solle, I'll leave them to you.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.180
Understood, Chief.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.070
So you've just started and you're already causing us trouble.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.140
Okay, Escha-kun.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:05.210
Even though you've already helped us quite a bit,

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:10.830
you are now an official alchemist of the Colseit Branch R&D Department.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.120
Please do your best to help Colseit Town.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.620
Yes, I'll do my best!

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:24.020
So you're already getting scolded by Solle-kun.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.800
I'm not really good around him, or should I say he's kind of always been strict with me.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:34.060
Yeah, since he's an accountant,

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.980
he probably sees those of us in the R&D department as useless and do nothing but weigh down the budget.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.150
Really?!

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.140
But not anymore.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:47.790
Starting today, we have two new alchemists in our ranks!

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:53.600
I'm still just a rookie who can't synthesize anything but really simple things.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.660
Huh? Did you say two alchemists, Marion-san?

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.760
Yeah, I did.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:02.990
Based on the regular flight schedule, he should be here soon.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:06.230
If I recall correctly, there's a flight arriving from Central City today.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.220
Yep, that's right.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.340
Pardon me.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:21.720
Pleasure to meet you.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:25.230
I am Logix Fiscario, the alchemist sent here from Central City.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.740
Please call me Logy.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.210
I'm Marion, the R&D Department's manager.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.620
And she is...

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.880
I-I'm Escha-

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:42.790
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.340
A s-sword?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.720
Yes, I was told that weapons are necessary in remote areas.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:49.540
I-I guess that's true.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:53.220
You would need them when you go exploring.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.840
Right, Escha-chan?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:58.970
Escha-chan?

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.170
What's wrong, Escha-chan?

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.810
I'm sorry I panicked.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:08.610
No, I'm the one who should apologise.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:13.020
Okay, you two, I'll show you your atelier.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.440
Oh, please do.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:15.510
Yes!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.050
It's a cauldron!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.620
You got us a new one!

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:29.730
That's right.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:34.480
We prepared one since we got two new alchemists.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.020
Speaking of which...

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:41.160
That's... a cauldron?

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.220
Logy-kun?

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.930
Oh, excuse me.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.230
I'm just surprised.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.290
I see.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:49.060
You're not used to such a remote area yet, after all.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.820
Since we're here, why don't you try to make something with alchemy?

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:59.080
I'm sorry, but I can't use a cauldron to synthesize.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.250
Huh? How come?

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:04.960
I've never used a cauldron to perform traditional alchemy.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.960
Huh? Really?

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.260
Yeah.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:11.320
It's quite different in Central City.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:15.970
We use something like this.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.140
I see.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.770
I made a mistake due to my lack of knowledge.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.070
I'll ask the branch chief to procure new equipment.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.860
May I have a moment?

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:32.450
Since all of us from the R&D Department are here, may I try making something?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.470
But everyone's not here yet...

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.000
Is something wrong?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.370
Oh, nothing.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.330
Go ahead, Escha-chan.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.290
Yes!

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.110
Wait just half an hour.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.500
Okay! It's finished!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.050
Here, the Apple Tart is done!

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:34.870
Apple Tart?

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.420
You just... made a tart... in that cauldron?

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.180
I have tea too.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.310
I-I'll have some.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.280
It's delicious.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.360
Thank goodness!

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:07.060
I submitted the request for the Central City-style equipment to the branch chief.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:10.400
We should get all of the equipment by next week at the earliest.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.210
Thank you so much.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.800
But I can't let you do nothing until then.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:21.390
There's no point in having a R&D branch if we're unable to show the public that we're meeting their needs.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.870
Here's your first assignment.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:27.210
The two of you should work together to get the job done.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.460
Yes.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:31.040
Well, then, your first job is...

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:33.990
...to fix the windmill at the apple orchard.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.700
The apple orchard's... windmill?

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.780
Is that really something the R&D division should be doing?

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:41.740
Yes, it is.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:45.080
And it's a very important task here in Colseit.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:45.960
But...

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.180
We don't have time for your complaints.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.790
Now, get going.

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.000
Understood.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.390
I know I said that, but I don't think I can accept it.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.210
Really?

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:08.480
Even with that, this is still Colseit's Frontier Special Investigation Bureau.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.100
I wonder if an assignment like this is really okay.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:15.820
It's true that this is a remote area, so I understand it's not as busy around here, but...

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:18.800
You can just call me Escha, Logy-san.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.150
You were surprised as well, weren't you, Escha?

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:25.280
Yes, but I was surprised for a different reason.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:29.840
The apple orchard is my home.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.200
Hey, Escha-chan!

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.720
Good afternoon, Duke-san!

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.670
Stop by after you're done working!

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.280
Sure!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.230
Escha, you're with someone I don't recognise.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.860
Yes, this is Logy-san.  He's from Central City.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.950
Looks like a nice guy.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:07.620
Don't bother them while they are working.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.360
Everyone knows you.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.690
Colseit's a small town, after all.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.090
Yeah, I did some research before I came.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:19.800
I heard this area used to be a desert.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:21.280
That's right.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:25.260
This place has been a desert according to all of our records.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:28.880
But, regardless of how small it is, it's a town now.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.060
That's true.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:34.230
Even the balloon docks I arrived at have been well maintained.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:37.110
It's not something you would expect from a remote town.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.840
The Land of Dusk, huh?

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.120
Is that what you guys call it in Central?

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:46.070
Yeah.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:50.640
A dry and barren desert where no plants can grow.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:55.460
Most of the land in this world is part of the Land of Dusk.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:59.550
There's very little land that humans can live in.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:03.680
The era that we live in is just like the dusk itself.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.780
But we live here.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.160
As did my mother, and her mother.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:12.510
All of them lived here, on this land.

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:22.860
Something smells nice.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:28.690
There are two reasons why Colseit has grown into such a big town.

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.200
This is one of them.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.470
That's amazing.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.740
In Central City, we hear many different things about these remote areas,

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:58.180
but I've never seen or heard about an apple orchard this big.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:02.260
The apples from this orchard are Colseit's speciality.

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:08.700
I grew up hearing stories that this used to be a wasteland.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:14.140
But they kept on ploughing and watering the land for several hundred years,

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:17.480
and it eventually turned into what you see now.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:18.860
Several hundred years?

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.420
Escha, who did you learn that from?

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.420
Clone!

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.720
Escha, welcome home.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.950
Automaton?

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.010
Yep.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.900
I'm home, Clone!

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:39.240
My oh my, you are home early, Escha.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.110
Have you been fired already?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.240
Hey, how could you say that, Clone!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.900
We're here for work!

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.070
My oh my, that's unexpected.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.150
Who is this here?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.860
I'm Logy.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:53.900
Clone-san, this is a wonderful apple orchard.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.240
Thank you.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.120
Are you the one who started all of this?

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:01.370
Allow me to give you a tour.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:21.280
You asked me earlier if I started the apple orchard.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:28.650
Yes, since you are an automaton that has lived for several hundred years, you might've started the orchard.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.360
My oh my, you are a bit mistaken there.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:35.830
It's true that I have been managing the orchard,

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:42.080
but humans were the ones to plough the land and plant and water the trees.

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:47.910
Escha's mother, her mother, and her mother all lived with me.

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:54.300
It's thanks to all the people who had lived up until now that the orchard has grown to this scale.

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:00.890
That is why you must also do your best.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:04.440
This is an important windmill used to pump groundwater.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.980
Please repair it.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.040
How is it?

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.060
The axle cracked.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:27.350
Do you think we can fix it?

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.360
Let me ask Onii-chan.

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:32.500
Onii-chan?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.260
Maintenance's Awin-san.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:37.890
He's my cousin, and he knows a lot about machines.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.290
I see.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.850
Also, there's not enough oil in the shaft.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.090
I'll look for the recipe.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:46.250
Tell me if there are any ingredients you need.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.580
Yes!

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.140
Is something on my face?

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:52.190
There's some oil on your cheek.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.200
Thank you.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:02.220
As an alchemist who came all the way from Central City,

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:07.970
I feel kind of bad making you help me fix my family's orchard all of a sudden.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.000
Don't worry about it.

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:13.060
This orchard is very important to Colseit.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:16.400
So this assignment is obviously something the branch should handle.

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:23.140
How is it, Onii-chan?

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:29.150
It's a special alloy, but you should be able to fix it if you have the right ingredients.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.040
Really?

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:33.720
Hey there. I'm Heizman, the chief of Maintenance.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:36.430
Want to work for me?

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:38.680
No, I'm also in R&D.

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:39.730
That's right.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:42.740
We just started working together.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:43.790
Okay.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.290
Do your best, you two.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.290
Thanks!

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:16.780
Is this all we need?

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.170
Yes, that should be it.

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:19.780
Okay.

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:21.410
Let's get started!

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:35.260
Now we just need to wait an hour.

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:38.480
Who did you learn alchemy from, Escha?

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.920
My mother.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.830
Has your entire family been alchemists?

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.100
It seems like it.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:49.660
My mother died when I was still young, so I only learned a tiny bit from her.

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.610
Other than that, Clone taught me a little.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.030
Well, she has lived for quite a while, so she probably knows a lot.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:59.380
Actually, Clone didn't dabble in alchemy all that much.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:04.950
That's why she pretty much just brought me the recipes that my mother left behind.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.040
I see.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:10.170
And how did you learn alchemy, Logy-san?

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.360
There's a school in Central City.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:18.080
In Central City, skilled Alchemists are in high demand.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:22.300
They want to recover ancient technologies and build new machines.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.510
Is that something you can do too, Logy-san?

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:25.730
I...

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:29.740
No, never mind.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:35.820
Here, alchemy is used for even the tiniest daily trifles.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:41.940
It's as if the alchemy in Central City is completely different than the alchemy here despite having the same name.

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.380
How is it?

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.710
A complete success!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.580
Yay! We did it!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.600
We did it...

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.050
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.150
Okay, it's good to go!

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.260
Roger!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.080
It's not moving?!

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.330
The wind's not blowing yet.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.040
But...!

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:31.230
Relax.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.190
It should turn when the wind picks up.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:34.120
Is there a window here?

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.210
Over here.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:47.870
It's turning!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:48.970
It's turning!

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.480
The parts are holding up fine too!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.590
Yes, it's a success!

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:56.410
See? Didn't I tell you it would turn when the wind picks up.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:57.860
It did!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:06.510
Logy-san, there's another reason for Colseit's prosperity.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.030
Yeah.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.400
The Unexplored Ruins.

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.300
That's right.

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:18.380
These are ruins suspended in midair that nobody has ever stepped foot on yet.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:24.600
It is said that the balloon docks were built so that we could explore those ruins.

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.510
However, nobody has been there.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:33.100
Yes, I heard balloons can't reach it because of the air turbulence and the floating rocks around it.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:38.990
Without another form of transportation, we won't be able to get there.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.650
Another form of transportation, huh?

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.570
It's my dream.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:49.530
Ever since I was a kid, it's been my dream to go to those ruins.

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:52.120
It would be great if you get there.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:53.140
Yes!

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:33.430
What's a Mage?
